# Physical controller source assets

The `*.sh` files and `resourceclaims.yaml` capture the older physical KUKA deployment flow:

- POST a `KukaController`
- patch the generated `Robot` CR with `resourceClaimName`

`deployment/deploy.py --mode physical` now reads these files as input data and emits the newer
DRANET-capable `network_interface` API payload instead, so the direct-network configuration is
declared through the NOVA API rather than patched into the `Robot` CR afterwards.
=== ir360r01.sh ===
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

if [[ $# -lt 1 ]]; then
  cat >&2 <<'USAGE'
Usage: ir360r01.sh [--virtual] [--slow-cycle-rate] [--access-token TOKEN] --network-interface IFNAME <nova-api-endpoint>

--network-interface is required for physical controllers (SR-IOV PF name,
node-qualified on multi-node clusters, e.g. wandelbox-wc5cl2-enp10s0f1).
USAGE
  exit 1
fi

exec bash "$(dirname "$0")/create-kuka-controller.sh" \
  "$@" \
  ir360r01 \
  25.85.121.200 \
  25.85.122.251 \
  30161 \
  25.85.121.251/24,25.85.122.251/24
